# Nissan Bluebird T12 four-door notchback saloon, 1985-1986.
#
# The T12 is a rebadged Nissan Auster, not the Japanese-market U11 Bluebird,
# and it has a different nose and roofline from that car. Introduced in Europe in
# 1985 and imported into Britain until production moved to Washington, Tyne and
# Wear in July 1986, when the same body became the T72.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nissan_Violet
#
# Dimensions 4.400 x 1.690 x 1.395 m, wheelbase 2.550 m, four-door notchback
# saloon. Sources: engineindetail's T12/T72 data and the English Wikipedia T12
# section, which agree on 4,400-4,460 mm length, 1,690 mm width, 1,395 mm height
# and 2,550 mm wheelbase. Side indicators take the modelled width to 1.702 m.
#
# Colours. No UK colour chart for the T12 was located, so the objects carry
# plain colour names: silver, blue, red and white. Weights silver 3, blue 3,
# red 2, white 2, total 10, provisional pending the central rebase.
#
# Speed 175 km/h for the 1.8, the volume UK engine. Comfort 80/450, on the line
# 330 + 1.5 x 80, a step above the rear-wheel-drive 910's 65/428. Classes 1,2.
#
# Dates are road presence: January 1985 intro, retires staggered 2001-2004 on a
# fifteen- to nineteen-year tail.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/nissan-bluebird-t12.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/nissan-bluebird-t12.dae (48 objects). References:
# citycars/references/nissan-bluebird-t12/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
# This master is the basis of the T72, which shares the shell.
#
# Accepted deviations: the bumper and corner shapes are simplified. The wheels
# are 0.580 m diameter, correct for the car's 13-inch fitment, and the
# photographed wheelbase/length ratio of 0.575 agrees with the published 0.580.
# At 128 px the notchback roofline, the rectangular lamps and the broad tail
# lamps read correctly.

obj=citycar
name=NissanBluebirdT12(Silver)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=3
intro_year=1985
intro_month=1
retire_year=2004
retire_month=6
speed=175
class=1,2
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=80
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=450

